  "known_limitations": [
    "SUPERSEDED by tools/aiworkhub/eval/aiworkhub_dynamic_worker_mcp_authority_repair_b834_v1.json: the original B833 candidate bound ENV_REPO (isolated worktree) as the ONLY repository binding, so a gitignored/absent worktree-local index database silently degraded a call toward hit_count=0 while still reporting ok=true. B834 adds a second, immutable AIWORKHUB_WORKER_MCP_AUTHORITY_REPO binding (the coordinator-owned host repository, read-only under both sandbox backends) that every Source Graph/Session Manager/AI Memory/KB call now reads from instead; an absent or empty authority database is now a hard, fail-closed violation rather than a silently-empty success.",
    "local validation in a nested Task-MCP-sandboxed worker session cannot exercise chmod/fchmod-dependent code paths (seccomp denies chmod family syscalls for a sandboxed worker, matching worker_workspace._probe_exec_capable_dir's own documented anticipation of this); tests mute os.chmod/os.fchmod the same way the existing test_worker_ai_infra_context_b437_v1.py suite already does. This is a pre-existing, environment-level condition (also affects test_worker_project_context_b434_v1.py, which this task does not own) and not something introduced here."
  ]
